user
You are controlling a single Panda arm in the LIBERO simulator through a local HTTP bridge.

Read obs/state.json and the two camera images every turn before you act:
- obs/agentview.png  third-person view of the table
- obs/wrist.png      eye-in-hand / gripper camera
- obs/state.json     instruction plus current grasp-point state

HTTP API (localhost only):
  GET  http://127.0.0.1:8765/status
  POST http://127.0.0.1:8765/move      JSON body
  POST http://127.0.0.1:8765/give_up   JSON {"reason": "..."}

move JSON:
{
  "x": <meters, world +x>,
  "y": <meters, world +y>,
  "z": <meters, world +z, up>,
  "gripper": <0 closed, 1 open>,
  "note": "<one or two sentences: what you see and why this motion>"
}
Name only the dimensions you want to change. Unnamed x/y/z/gripper keep the current observed value.
You may also send dx/dy/dz instead of absolute x/y/z.

Rules:
1. The language instruction in state.json is the only goal. Official LIBERO success is the only success signal; do not declare success yourself.
2. Estimate object positions from RGB. There is no depth, no object pose, no layout JSON.
3. Work in small motions. Full-size reaches belong in free space. Once the gripper is within about 2 cm of the object or table, use a few millimetres per call and re-read the cameras.
4. Grasp-point is between the jaws. Table objects sit below the current eef_z (home is about z=1.18). Lower z to reach the table; do not command z far below ~0.82 or you will hit the table.
5. gripper 1 = open, 0 = closed. Close only when the jaws surround the object.
6. After a pick, lift at least 5–8 cm before translating laterally, then place.
7. One POST /move per turn. Then read the new images and state.json.
8. Stop when state.json has "success": true or "terminated": true, or when remaining_moves / remaining_env_steps hits 0.
9. If you cannot finish, POST /give_up with a short reason.
10. Do not install packages, do not change bridge_server.py, do not kill the server.
11. When the episode ends, write a short markdown file at runs/current/AGENT_SUMMARY.md covering: what you tried, where it failed or succeeded, and what you would change next time.

Use curl. Example:
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8765/status
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8765/move -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"z": 1.05, "gripper": 1, "note": "Raise for a clear approach."}'

Begin now: GET /status, look at both images, then move.

